For example, in rule ("ab", 1, 2), string "ab" has 1 occurrence in "ab", so it complies with this rule (since 1 is between 1 and 2 inclusive). But for rule ("cd", 1, 2), "ab" has 0 occurrences in "cd", so it doesn't comply (since 0 < 1).

Now, our goal is: given string s, and n rules each of which is (p, l, r), count the number of distinct substrings t of s that are good (i.e., for every rule (p, l, r), |occurrences of t in p| ∈ [l, r]).

