But how to check a rule (p, l, r) for a substring t?

To compute the number of occurrences of t in p: let's call it occ(p, t).

If t is longer than p, then occ(p, t) = 0 (for example, if |t| > |p|, then t can't occur in p, so 0 occurrences).

But in our case, for a substring t of s (which is up to length 50,000), and p can be up to length 50,000 (max length of p is ≤ 50,000), so if |t| > |p|, then occ(p, t) = 0.

