So for each rule (p, l, r) and candidate t (which is a substring of s):

- If m = |t| > |p|: occ = 0.
  - then if l > 0: t does not comply with this rule.
  - else (l == 0): then occ = 0 ∈ [0, r] (since r ≥ l = 0, so 0 ≤ r), so complies with this rule.

